WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.950
(fast piano music)

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.100
- [Narrator] At first glance

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.580
you might think that
these were photographs.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.710
But these are pencil drawings

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.513
part of a growing art
movement called hyperrealism.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.510
- When people look at my drawings

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.989
I would love them to
feel a sense of emotion,

00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:19.771
a reality, you know.

00:00:19.771 --> 00:00:22.263
These are my works to
bring people down to earth.

00:00:23.761 --> 00:00:26.344
(upbeat music)

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.636
My name is Arinze Stanley.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:40.823
I am hyperrealistic artist.

00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:44.315
Hyperrealism is a genre
of art that involves

00:00:44.315 --> 00:00:49.193
making drawings or paintings
that looks very realistic.

00:00:49.193 --> 00:00:52.400
And you can't actually distinguish it

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.173
from a photograph or reality.

00:00:56.946 --> 00:00:59.980
I started drawing when I was 6 years old.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.900
My dad owns a paper factory.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.870
I basically grew up around

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:04.863
a lot of paper.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.050
When people see my works,

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.060
they are usually shocked
that it is not a photo.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.718
They go like, "Oh wow,

00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:15.640
"is that a photo?"

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.810
Did you make that with a pencil?

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.345
And I'm like, "Yeah."
(laughing)

00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:22.178
(upbeat music)

00:01:22.178 --> 00:01:24.680
Usually, my works take
a long time to create.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.120
Sometimes, I can make a
piece for about a month.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.330
Sometimes it could drag
onto two months depending

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:34.653
on my mood and the size of the piece.

00:01:36.091 --> 00:01:38.590
(upbeat piano music)
I like to use

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.710
my works to speak on
issues affecting my society

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.710
here in Nigeria and the whole of Africa.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.320
Use the voice that I have
through my art to speak

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.150
for people who can't speak for themselves.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.825
This person is totally engulfed in oil.

00:01:55.825 --> 00:01:58.457
This signifies how much we use oil

00:01:58.457 --> 00:02:01.570
and destroy our society.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.818
This signifies the see no evil,

00:02:04.818 --> 00:02:07.245
hear no evil and speak no evil.

00:02:07.245 --> 00:02:10.385
I'm encouraging people to take a step back

00:02:10.385 --> 00:02:13.221
and try to emulate their childhood.

00:02:13.221 --> 00:02:16.373
Trying to make people reset to default.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.514
When I pick up my pencil

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.054
and put it on paper,

00:02:21.054 --> 00:02:23.200
it takes me away.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.363
It's something I can't explain in words.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:33.020
(slow upbeat music)

